1
00:01:15,533 --> 00:01:17,786
Today's regular
is Mr. Chang-sik.

2
00:01:17,869 --> 00:01:20,246
Driver, would you like some tteokbokki?

3
00:01:21,831 --> 00:01:22,916
By day, he helps his father

4
00:01:22,999 --> 00:01:24,793
with his work at Sewoon Plaza.

5
00:01:24,876 --> 00:01:28,379
At night, I work as a DJ
under the name 'Jacky Jacky.'

6
00:01:30,089 --> 00:01:31,466
- Thanks for the meal.
- Enjoy.

7
00:01:31,549 --> 00:01:32,592
Yes.

8
00:01:33,510 --> 00:01:36,012
Chang-sik and I
get along pretty well.

9
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:42,811
We're more than

10
00:01:42,894 --> 00:01:46,189
driver and passenger.
You could say we talk music.

11
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:49,400
I don't usually lend my records

12
00:01:49,484 --> 00:01:52,195
to anyone, but

13
00:01:53,363 --> 00:01:55,824
I trust you, Chang-sik,
so I'm lending you one.

14
00:01:56,783 --> 00:01:58,409
I don't mean to pressure you, but

15
00:01:59,077 --> 00:02:00,703
if this gets scratched,

16
00:02:01,412 --> 00:02:03,581
our relationship gets scratched too.
You know that, right?

17
00:02:03,665 --> 00:02:05,875
Driver, I'm a DJ.

18
00:02:05,959 --> 00:02:08,336
You know I don't even breathe
when I handle records!

19
00:02:08,962 --> 00:02:09,796
Thank you.

20
00:02:15,426 --> 00:02:16,386
Thank you.

21
00:02:17,804 --> 00:02:19,472
Wow, Sanullim's third album.

22
00:02:22,392 --> 00:02:23,726
- Woah!
- Yeah, yeah.

23
00:02:26,688 --> 00:02:28,356
'Rock Music'

24
00:02:28,439 --> 00:02:32,610
'Remake'

25
00:02:37,073 --> 00:02:39,492
Everything has changed
a great deal.

26
00:02:43,454 --> 00:02:45,415
But even so,

27
00:02:45,498 --> 00:02:47,917
it's fun to find the things
that haven't changed.

28
00:02:51,045 --> 00:02:53,172
Those are new glasses.
Haven't seen them before.

29
00:02:53,256 --> 00:02:55,508
Did you get those at Dongmyo, too?

30
00:02:55,592 --> 00:02:56,593
No.

31
00:02:56,676 --> 00:02:59,888
You don't always find something you like
at Dongmyo.

32
00:03:01,222 --> 00:03:04,601
There are so many people
looking for vintage these days

33
00:03:05,184 --> 00:03:07,729
that there are lots of new clothes
made to look vintage.

34
00:03:11,190 --> 00:03:13,192
Maybe it was untouched by time?

35
00:03:15,820 --> 00:03:18,656
Wearing clothes someone else has
worn just feels a little icky.

36
00:03:19,490 --> 00:03:22,285
I'm buying someone else's memories.

37
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:26,539
I believe objects hold memories, too.

38
00:03:27,540 --> 00:03:30,793
But things straight from the factory
haven't made any memories yet.

39
00:03:31,377 --> 00:03:34,589
Finding something with memories
that fits

40
00:03:34,672 --> 00:03:38,259
and that you like
can't be easy.

41
00:03:39,010 --> 00:03:40,094
That's right.

42
00:03:40,178 --> 00:03:42,430
So I usually come back empty-handed.

43
00:03:42,513 --> 00:03:44,015
But when that happens,

44
00:03:44,098 --> 00:03:46,309
I just get a bowl of janchi-guksu
before heading home.

45
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:53,316
Driver, take a look at this.

46
00:03:53,399 --> 00:03:54,234
Yes.

47
00:03:57,403 --> 00:04:00,073
Oh, Mr. Chang-sik, you play guitar too?

48
00:04:00,156 --> 00:04:01,741
That's a photo of my father.

49
00:04:02,533 --> 00:04:03,618
Pardon?

50
00:04:03,701 --> 00:04:05,495
Wait, this...

51
00:04:05,578 --> 00:04:07,372
Even the clothes he's wearing...

52
00:04:07,455 --> 00:04:08,748
They're identical.

53
00:04:08,831 --> 00:04:10,458
Well, this was a few days ago.

54
00:04:12,835 --> 00:04:15,338
I came home one day after buying
a few used records.

55
00:04:18,091 --> 00:04:18,925
In our yard,

56
00:04:19,008 --> 00:04:20,802
there was a huge pile of clothes.

57
00:04:25,431 --> 00:04:26,266
Oh, that's pretty.

58
00:04:29,811 --> 00:04:30,979
What are you doing over there?

59
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:35,233
Hey, take all these clothes
and dump them in the clothing bin.

60
00:04:35,316 --> 00:04:37,026
They're too heavy for me to carry.

61
00:04:37,110 --> 00:04:38,194
Mom, where did all these come from?

62
00:04:38,278 --> 00:04:39,696
Where do you think?

63
00:04:39,779 --> 00:04:42,490
They're your dad's old clothes.
Some are decades old.

64
00:04:42,573 --> 00:04:44,200
I've been telling him to throw them out!

65
00:04:44,284 --> 00:04:46,119
I've been telling him for
years to get rid of them,

66
00:04:46,202 --> 00:04:47,620
but your dad is so cheap,

67
00:04:47,704 --> 00:04:50,373
he practically shakes at the
thought of throwing anything away.

68
00:04:50,456 --> 00:04:52,750
Quick, get rid of them
while your dad's out.

69
00:04:52,834 --> 00:04:55,003
The closet's already packed to the brim.

70
00:04:55,086 --> 00:04:56,379
What year is it?

71
00:04:56,462 --> 00:04:58,339
Who keeps clothes like these around?
Honestly.

72
00:04:58,423 --> 00:04:59,716
Mom...

73
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:01,134
I want to wear this.

74
00:05:02,135 --> 00:05:03,886
It's pretty, right?

75
00:05:11,978 --> 00:05:13,813
I'm late. I'm late.

76
00:05:19,068 --> 00:05:20,320
Why am I at my own house?

77
00:05:20,903 --> 00:05:22,780
Well, it's my house. Of course I'm here.

78
00:05:22,864 --> 00:05:24,240
No!

79
00:05:24,324 --> 00:05:26,075
Why is my twenty-year-old self here?

80
00:05:26,159 --> 00:05:27,994
Put some clothes on!

81
00:05:28,077 --> 00:05:29,454
You never wear the clothes I buy you,

82
00:05:30,038 --> 00:05:32,415
and what is there to see?
Why walk around half-naked?

83
00:05:32,498 --> 00:05:33,875
You're humiliating me in front
of the whole neighborhood.

84
00:05:33,958 --> 00:05:34,792
Dad.

85
00:05:35,626 --> 00:05:36,753
It's me.

86
00:05:36,836 --> 00:05:37,754
Son?

87
00:05:37,837 --> 00:05:39,297
- Son.
- Son?

88
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:40,715
- Son.
- Son?

89
00:05:40,798 --> 00:05:41,632
Yes!

90
00:05:42,508 --> 00:05:43,342
This...

91
00:05:46,304 --> 00:05:47,346
Oh, this...

92
00:05:47,430 --> 00:05:49,015
Wait, hold on a second.

93
00:05:49,098 --> 00:05:50,516
- Why, why, why, why, why?
- Hey!

94
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:51,684
- Hold on.
- Yes, careful...

95
00:05:52,935 --> 00:05:55,146
Hurry up and throw it
away before I burn it.

96
00:05:55,229 --> 00:05:56,689
- Ah!
- I said throw it away.

97
00:05:56,773 --> 00:05:58,566
What are you doing in the meantime?

98
00:05:58,649 --> 00:06:00,151
- Hey! Hold still.
- Goodness.

99
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:02,612
- Son!
- Yes.

100
00:06:06,574 --> 00:06:08,534
These glasses

101
00:06:08,618 --> 00:06:10,495
will make you complete.

102
00:06:15,666 --> 00:06:16,793
Father.

103
00:06:36,729 --> 00:06:39,649
What a bunch of idiots.

104
00:06:57,667 --> 00:07:00,920
Looks like even a place like this has
a lounge bar with a DJ.

105
00:07:01,003 --> 00:07:02,672
Driver, that's the red sign.

106
00:07:06,509 --> 00:07:08,427
Driver, would you like to come in with me?

107
00:07:08,511 --> 00:07:12,348
The songs feel a little different
here than they do in the taxi.

108
00:07:18,521 --> 00:07:20,106
No, I, I can't.

109
00:07:20,189 --> 00:07:21,607
I have to work, yes.

110
00:07:40,668 --> 00:07:42,920
'Rock.'

111
00:08:34,764 --> 00:08:36,182
'Namee Chameleon'

112
00:08:56,077 --> 00:08:58,120
The Sanullim album you lent me

113
00:08:59,664 --> 00:09:01,290
It'll be the grand finale.

114
00:09:03,042 --> 00:09:04,919
Don't just give me that look.

115
00:09:05,586 --> 00:09:07,213
Go talk to her.

116
00:09:07,296 --> 00:09:08,422
Go...

117
00:09:10,508 --> 00:09:11,634
Excuse me, driver.

118
00:09:12,385 --> 00:09:15,680
When I'm working,
I never let my mind wander like that.

119
00:09:15,763 --> 00:09:21,519
♪ I knew from the very start ♪

120
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:34,782
♪ I'm not afraid anymore ♪

121
00:09:35,533 --> 00:09:39,662
♪ Even if you come closer to me ♪

122
00:09:40,329 --> 00:09:45,751
♪ Since I realized I like you too ♪

123
00:09:45,835 --> 00:09:47,712
I didn't order this.

124
00:09:47,795 --> 00:09:50,840
Our DJ, Jacky Jacky, bought it for you.

125
00:09:50,923 --> 00:09:53,634
♪ As I watch you ♪

126
00:09:53,718 --> 00:09:58,222
♪ As I look at you ♪

127
00:09:58,306 --> 00:10:00,558
♪ Oh-oh-oh-oh ♪

128
00:10:00,641 --> 00:10:06,480
♪ My heart, falling in love ♪

129
00:10:06,564 --> 00:10:08,941
♪ Had fallen in love ♪

130
00:10:09,025 --> 00:10:10,526
♪ Closer ♪

131
00:10:10,610 --> 00:10:11,652
Excuse me...

132
00:10:12,403 --> 00:10:14,113
Yes, yes.

133
00:10:14,196 --> 00:10:18,159
♪ My heart keeps pounding ♪

134
00:10:18,242 --> 00:10:19,535
May I touch it?

135
00:10:21,621 --> 00:10:22,455
Yes.

136
00:10:25,708 --> 00:10:27,793
No, I mean this record.

137
00:10:27,877 --> 00:10:28,961
Oh, the record.

138
00:10:29,045 --> 00:10:30,421
- Yes.
- Oh, right.

139
00:10:31,756 --> 00:10:33,674
Yes, yes.
Go ahead and handle it.

140
00:10:47,772 --> 00:10:49,940
You know your way around records.

141
00:10:50,024 --> 00:10:51,025
Yes.

142
00:10:51,108 --> 00:10:53,027
This, this first pressing...

143
00:10:53,110 --> 00:10:55,946
It was really hard to find in Korea.

144
00:10:56,030 --> 00:10:56,864
Back then, in Korea,

145
00:10:56,947 --> 00:10:59,825
they didn't press many
copies of this album.

146
00:10:59,909 --> 00:11:02,912
But it actually became
better known in the U.S.,

147
00:11:02,995 --> 00:11:05,790
so there are probably more people

148
00:11:05,873 --> 00:11:07,458
in the U.S. who own this album.

149
00:11:08,334 --> 00:11:11,587
- Right.
- But it's been reissued,

150
00:11:11,671 --> 00:11:14,090
so now you can easily buy it online...

151
00:11:14,173 --> 00:11:17,301
But the ones pressed these days...

152
00:11:17,385 --> 00:11:19,887
don't have the memories
of that time in them.

153
00:11:22,973 --> 00:11:24,100
Right.

154
00:11:26,394 --> 00:11:28,312
They don't have those memories in them.

155
00:11:29,772 --> 00:11:30,606
Yes.

156
00:11:35,069 --> 00:11:38,906
♪ My heart keeps trembling ♪

157
00:11:38,989 --> 00:11:40,866
♪ Oh, darling, tonight ♪

158
00:11:40,950 --> 00:11:42,701
- It tastes better with a straw.
- Yeah.

159
00:11:42,785 --> 00:11:44,912
♪ Just the two of us,
you and me, like this ♪

160
00:11:44,995 --> 00:11:46,163
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

161
00:11:46,247 --> 00:11:50,084
♪ I just want to stay with you ♪

162
00:11:50,167 --> 00:11:52,503
Hey, Chang-sik.
Honestly, I never understood

163
00:11:52,586 --> 00:11:55,005
why you went around like this.

164
00:11:55,089 --> 00:11:57,383
But seeing you DJ here today,

165
00:11:57,466 --> 00:11:58,592
I get it now.

166
00:11:58,676 --> 00:12:00,469
It suits you so well.

167
00:12:04,098 --> 00:12:05,433
I'll...

168
00:12:05,516 --> 00:12:06,934
Go get the car.

169
00:12:07,017 --> 00:12:08,269
What? Driver...

170
00:12:25,536 --> 00:12:27,121
The taxi...

171
00:12:27,872 --> 00:12:29,665
They're hard to find, aren't they?

172
00:12:29,748 --> 00:12:30,791
Yes.

173
00:12:46,307 --> 00:12:49,101
I hope you're not going out
of your way because of me.

174
00:12:49,185 --> 00:12:50,895
No, not at all.

175
00:12:50,978 --> 00:12:53,189
It's on my way anyway.

176
00:12:53,272 --> 00:12:54,356
It's really no trouble.

177
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:55,608
Right, driver?

178
00:12:57,151 --> 00:13:00,404
That's right.
We have to go through Suwon.

179
00:13:00,488 --> 00:13:01,530
Yes.

180
00:13:03,324 --> 00:13:06,744
I really enjoyed that gin and tonic today.

181
00:13:09,497 --> 00:13:10,414
Gin and tonic?

182
00:13:11,332 --> 00:13:14,210
But you said earlier
that the DJ bought it for me...

183
00:13:20,508 --> 00:13:21,592
Yes.

184
00:13:25,679 --> 00:13:26,805
And this taxi...

185
00:13:26,889 --> 00:13:29,558
You can request songs, too.

186
00:13:30,226 --> 00:13:31,936
Are you a DJ too, driver?

187
00:13:33,979 --> 00:13:34,813
Well, I just...

188
00:13:34,897 --> 00:13:37,149
I just listen to music with my passengers.

189
00:13:37,233 --> 00:13:39,235
Even albums I couldn't find...

190
00:13:39,318 --> 00:13:41,111
This driver has just about everything.

191
00:13:42,112 --> 00:13:44,740
Do you collect records too, driver?

192
00:13:44,823 --> 00:13:49,745
I don't discriminate between
cassettes, CDs, or records.

193
00:13:49,828 --> 00:13:52,915
You can never truly own music,

194
00:13:52,998 --> 00:13:55,000
but I like to keep it close.

195
00:13:55,084 --> 00:13:56,335
Rather than collecting records,

196
00:13:56,418 --> 00:13:59,296
'staying by the records'

197
00:13:59,380 --> 00:14:00,798
is a better way to put it.

198
00:14:12,101 --> 00:14:13,936
- I...
- Yes, here you go.

199
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:20,526
Um, earlier...

200
00:14:20,609 --> 00:14:22,987
What was the name of the
song you played at the shop?

201
00:14:23,070 --> 00:14:24,530
Yes.

202
00:14:25,239 --> 00:14:27,199
Namee's...

203
00:14:27,283 --> 00:14:28,659
'The One I Want to Be Close To'

204
00:14:28,742 --> 00:14:29,577
'You.'

205
00:14:30,870 --> 00:14:31,912
Pardon?

206
00:14:48,888 --> 00:14:52,766
♪ Just by looking into your eyes ♪

207
00:14:53,642 --> 00:14:58,647
♪ I can feel it ♪

208
00:14:58,731 --> 00:15:03,068
♪ That you like me ♪

209
00:15:03,152 --> 00:15:09,450
♪ I knew it from the very start ♪

210
00:15:18,292 --> 00:15:22,212
♪ I'm not afraid anymore ♪

211
00:15:23,005 --> 00:15:26,926
♪ Even if you come closer to me ♪

212
00:15:27,927 --> 00:15:34,099
♪ Since I realized
I like you, too ♪

213
00:15:34,183 --> 00:15:38,354
♪ Everything feels like a dream ♪

214
00:15:38,437 --> 00:15:41,106
♪ As I watch you ♪

215
00:15:41,190 --> 00:15:45,527
♪ Here by my side ♪

216
00:15:45,611 --> 00:15:48,113
♪ Ooh-ooh-ooh-ooh ♪

217
00:15:48,197 --> 00:15:53,953
♪ My heart has fallen in love ♪

218
00:15:54,036 --> 00:15:56,413
♪ I see ♪

219
00:15:57,873 --> 00:15:59,667
You don't all have to get out.

220
00:16:04,421 --> 00:16:06,382
Yes, yes...

221
00:16:13,013 --> 00:16:14,723
I had a lovely time today.

222
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:18,394
Yes, I really enjoyed it too.

223
00:16:30,614 --> 00:16:33,450
Please, go on in first.

224
00:16:33,534 --> 00:16:35,452
Yes, then.

225
00:16:38,539 --> 00:16:40,207
Yes, I'm sorry.

226
00:16:43,335 --> 00:16:44,336
Go on in.

227
00:16:44,420 --> 00:16:46,547
Yes, get home safe.

228
00:17:08,402 --> 00:17:09,611
Did you get her number?

229
00:17:17,202 --> 00:17:18,120
Here...

230
00:17:27,004 --> 00:17:30,174
I was worrying for nothing.

231
00:17:30,257 --> 00:17:31,550
Honestly, you guys...

232
00:17:34,470 --> 00:17:35,888
I'm so sorry.

233
00:17:58,869 --> 00:17:59,787
Thank you.

234
00:18:07,127 --> 00:18:08,587
I didn't even play that today.

235
00:18:09,171 --> 00:18:10,464
Well, still...

236
00:18:10,547 --> 00:18:12,341
If there's a disagreement later,

237
00:18:12,424 --> 00:18:14,259
we'll end up on bad terms.

238
00:18:16,512 --> 00:18:17,346
Yes.

239
00:18:21,475 --> 00:18:25,395
♪ J, a beautiful summer day ♪

240
00:18:25,479 --> 00:18:27,314
♪ Far away... ♪

241
00:18:27,397 --> 00:18:28,857
Father.

242
00:18:29,525 --> 00:18:30,400
Son!

243
00:18:30,484 --> 00:18:31,819
Wait.

244
00:18:32,820 --> 00:18:35,864
Those are new clothes and a hat.

245
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:40,744
My son took all his father's clothes,

246
00:18:40,828 --> 00:18:41,954
so I had to buy new ones.

247
00:18:42,037 --> 00:18:43,247
Come on, Dad.

248
00:18:43,330 --> 00:18:46,375
I saved these clothes
from going up in flames.

249
00:18:48,085 --> 00:18:49,753
Is something important happening today?

250
00:18:50,587 --> 00:18:52,047
My son,

251
00:18:52,131 --> 00:18:55,634
In our lives, there isn't a
single day that doesn't matter.

252
00:18:58,554 --> 00:18:59,847
Son.

253
00:18:59,930 --> 00:19:02,432
You'll get chewed out by your
mom if you go in now anyway.

254
00:19:03,308 --> 00:19:04,935
Why not just come home even later?

255
00:19:06,979 --> 00:19:08,647
That's the most important thing.

256
00:19:24,454 --> 00:19:25,289
Son.

257
00:19:26,165 --> 00:19:28,083
How's your love life going?

258
00:19:30,878 --> 00:19:33,630
I told you to learn guitar already.

259
00:19:34,715 --> 00:19:36,633
There's something I really want
to show you.

260
00:19:41,680 --> 00:19:43,432
- This isn't it.
- Hey, hold still. Let me see.

261
00:19:43,515 --> 00:19:44,516
Give it here. Let me see.

262
00:19:50,731 --> 00:19:52,941
Oh, this...

263
00:19:55,944 --> 00:20:00,616
♪ J, my love ♪

264
00:20:00,699 --> 00:20:07,289
♪ Hasn't changed at all ♪

265
00:20:07,372 --> 00:20:09,666
♪ J ♪

266
00:20:09,750 --> 00:20:14,296
♪ I can't forget you ♪

267
00:20:15,422 --> 00:20:16,882
♪ J ♪

268
00:20:16,965 --> 00:20:18,467
Please stop playing the guitar.

269
00:20:18,550 --> 00:20:20,260
You're keeping the neighbors up.

270
00:20:20,344 --> 00:20:21,970
So...

271
00:20:22,054 --> 00:20:23,972
Until you give me your house number...

272
00:20:24,056 --> 00:20:26,183
I'm not moving an inch
from here.

273
